<<<
jollily, jolly adv. As a slang substitute for very (a j. good hiding; you know j. well) the adverb is jolly; in other uses (he smiled j. enough) it is jollily. See -LILY.
===
**jollily, jolly** adv. As a slang substitute for very (*a j. good hiding; you know j. well*) the adverb is *jolly*; in other uses (*he smiled j. enough*) it is *jollily*. See ^^-LILY^^.
>>>

